      "eventMetadata": {
        "context_description": "US and Israeli airstrikes on Iranian targets since February 2026, including the elimination of Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei, have shifted toward sustained air and naval operations, economic sanctions under the new “Operation Economic Outcast,” and a naval blockade of the Strait of Hormuz rather than ground forces. A June memorandum of understanding mediated by Pakistan produced only a fragile, repeatedly violated ceasefire, with both sides trading limited strikes into August amid stalled talks through Oman. Military analysts and former commanders assess a large-scale US ground invasion as highly improbable due to prohibitive troop requirements, logistical challenges, and risks of prolonged entanglement, leading traders to assign an 87.5% probability that no invasion occurs before the end of 2026.",
